      "textEn": "365\n\nMeaning: Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti has explained the thoughts of the Gopis as follows: \"Perhaps these\ntrees and vines (which are mentioned in the previous verses) did not hear our questions because they\nwere absorbed in the meditation of Lord Vishnu. Or maybe, because they don't want to tell us where Krishna has gone,\nthey are hard-hearted even while living in a holy place. Whatever it may be, what is the benefit of unnecessarily criticizing the residents of this holy place? We cannot say whether they truly know where Krishna has gone. So let's see if we can find someone who knows where they are.” This\nIn this way, the Gopis concluded that since Krishna has to be somewhere on this earth, therefore the earth\nmust know about them. Then the Gopis thought, \"Since Krishna always wanders on earth, therefore the earth never\nseparates from him, therefore she cannot understand how much suffering their parents,\nfriends, and servants endure in his absence.\"\n\n.\n\nOh, friend Hirani, did the God Achyut, who bestows supreme bliss upon your eyes, come here with his beloved? In fact, the fragrance of that garland made of kund flowers on this side is\nremaining, which was coated with kumkum applied on the breasts of her beloved friend, who was embraced by her. Meaning: Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti has given the following enchanting commentary on this verse:\nThe Gopis asked Hiranya, \"O Sakhi Hiranya!\" The joy in your serene eyes, from that we"
