      "textEn": "369\n\nVatsayati hanti chaanya tatraika tu bakayati. 17. Meaning of the word\n\nKrishna-Ramayite—Becoming Krishna and Balarama; Dwe—Two Gopis; Tu—Thus; Gopayantya—Becoming like the cowherds; Cha—\nThus; Kashchan—Someone; Vatsayatim—Becoming Vatsasura; Hanti—Killed; Cha—Thus; Anya—Other; Tatra—There; Eka—One;\nTu—And also; Bakayatim—Acting like Bakasura. Two Gopis became Ram and Krishna among all those Gopis who were acting as cowherds.\nThey were acting. A Gopi imitated the killing of the demon Vatsasura by Krishna, in which the second\nGopi became Vatsasura. A pair of gopis enacted the scene of Bakasura's slaying. Aahuyah, from where the darkness follows.\nThey play with the flute, others sing praises of the virtuous. 18. Meaning of the word\n\nAahuya—calling; Door—at a distance; Gaah—to the cows; Yadvat—as; Krishna—Krishna; Tam—that; Anuvartati—following;\nAnuakaran karne wali Gopi ko; Veenam—Vanshi; Kwanntim—making sounds; Kridantim—playing; Anyah—other Gopis\nNe; Shansanti—praised; Sadhu iti—Very good!When a Gopi completely imitated how Krishna used to wander far away,\nhow he used to call the cows, how he used to play the flute, and how he used to engage in various games,\nthen others cheered very well, very well, (wow wow). Having fixed his own body,\nHe moves, like a shadow.\nKrishna, I see the path.\nLalita, thus the mind is absorbed. 19. Meaning of the word\n\nKasyanchit—Of one of them; Swa-bhujam—One's own arm; Nyasya—(on) the shoulder; Chalanti—Walking; Aah—Said;\nApara—Other; Nanu—Indeed; Krishna—Krishna; Aham—I am; Pashyat—Just look; Gatim—My gait; Lalitam—Beautiful;\nIti—With these words; Tat—In them; Manah—Completely absorbed; with a mind..\n\nAnother Gopi, fixing her mind on Krishna, placed her arm on the shoulder of another friend\nand started walking, saying, \"I am Krishna.\" Just look at me, how gracefully I am walking.\"\n\nMa bhāistha vātavarṣābhyāmyāt tratrāṇam viṇhitam maya. Having thus, with his own hands, he lifted the garment and placed it on his head. 20. Lexicon"
