      "textEn": "382\n\nIt rises. My body will become healthy again, and my life will automatically return to my body.\nAnd it will remain in my body.\"\n\n\"But you know the way to the forest without my help, so why did you order me this\nPrince and very young and gentle boy. He should have been respected.\nIt was necessary. Why did you order that you could take it wherever you wanted? Why did you make me so angry?\nWhy did you make me like this?“\n\nRadha shouts, \"Please, show your face to your humble servant.\" Have mercy on me! Be kind. When I gave you the order, I was overcome by sleep. I was tired of playing with you. Therefore, please forgive what your maidservant said. Please don't be rude. Because you treated me like such a close friend, although I was not worthy of it, that's why I said that to you.\"\n\"\n\"Okay, dear! I am very pleased with you, so come to me.“\n\n“But I have become blind with remorse.\nI can't see where you are. Tell me,\nWhere are you?Sreesuka said\n\nSreesuka said\nAnvichyantyo Bhagavato Margam Gopyo Aviduritah. Dadrushu priyavishleshanmoohitam duhkitam sakhi. 40. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Anvichintyah—searching; Bhagavatam—of the Lord; Margam—path;\nGopayah—by the Gopis; Aviduritah—not far, near; Dadrushah—saw; Priya—from one's beloved; Anleeshat—due to separation;\nMohitam—attached; Dukhitam—sorrowful; Sakhiam—to one's own friend. Shukdev Goswami said: The Gopis, searching for Krishna's path, found their sorrowful friend nearby. She was infatuated with the separation from her lover. Therefore, hearing this, one attains the desired honor, O Madhava. They were filled with disgust, wonder, and awe. 41. Lexicon"
