      "textEn": "383\n\nBy him—through him; said—what was said; unheard—heard; respect—of respect; attainment—attainment; and—and;\nFrom Madhava—from Krishna; disrespect—disrespect; and—and; from one's own behavior—from one's own misbehavior; astonishment—astonishment; supreme—very; experienced—experienced. He told them that Madhav had given him so much respect, but now\nhe had to face disrespect because of his misbehavior. The Gopis were very surprised to hear this. Meaning: It was natural for Radharani to ask Krishna to pick her up and take her away because this\nrequest was in accordance with their love relationship. But now, out of extreme humility, she calls her behavior\ncunning. Hearing these words, the other gopis were astonished. Then the moonlight, like the moon, is visible.\nTamaha praveshmalaakshya tato nivavrittaah striyah. 42. Meaning of the word\n\nTatah—Then; Avishan—Entered; Vanam—In the jungle; Chandra—Of the moon; Jyotsna—Moonlight; Yavat—Until; Vibhavyate—Were visible; Tamah—Darkness; Pravishtam—Entered; Aalakshya—Having seen; Tatah—Thereafter; Nivavrutuha—Became free;\nStriah—Women. Thereafter, the Gopis went as far into the forest in search of Krishna as far as the moon\nwas moonlight. But when they saw themselves surrounded by darkness, they decided to return.\nThey decided to return. Meaning: The Gopis had reached such a dense part of the forest where even the light of the full moon could not enter. In the Vishnu Purana, this scene is also described:\n\nEntering deeply, Krishna's feet are not visible. Nivartadhvam shashankasya naitad diidhigorah. “A Gopi said: “Krishna has entered such a dense part of the forest that we cannot even see his\nfootsteps.\nTherefore, we should return from this area, where even moonlight cannot reach,\nwe should walk.”\n\n[^1]: Tanmanaskaastadalapastadvichyeshtaastadatmikaah. [^2]: Those who sing with such qualities, remember their own self. 43. Lexicon"
